00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Animation Time Rectangle Marker

88
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
In animation projects, time control is important.

89
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
These markers are like the numbers on the time axis.

90
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Let's learn how to use these markers to simplify your production process.

91
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
First, we need to enter the bottom of the screen.

92
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
We need to enter the animation editor at the bottom of the screen.

93
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Check the time axis and the area that shows your real number.

94
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,000
If you want to add a precise moment to view and mark the animation,

95
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:15,000
All you need to do is right-click on the time axis and click on the animation mark group in the right menu.

96
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
At this time, an animation mark dialogue box will pop up.

97
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You can specify a specific name for the mark here.

98
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
For example, from here, and you can set a precise real number.

99
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
After pressing OK, stop the mouse on the mark indicator.

100
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
You will see a pop-up window.

101
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,000
It contains a specific name and position for quick reference.

102
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
If you want to edit the animation mark,

103
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,000
You can right-click it and select Edit or Double-click.

104
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
By dragging the mark, you can adjust its position.

105
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
To copy, paste and delete the animation mark,

106
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,000
You can right-click the animation mark again and select the operation you need.

107
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Or use the shortcut Ctrl-C, Ctrl-V and Delete to speed up the operation.

108
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
